Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:15:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: Support R32G32B32 uniform texel buffers

Metal has no texel buffer formats with three components, and D3D12
requires R32G32B32 typed buffer SRVs: Rise of the Tomb Raider's benchmark
creates R32G32B32_SFLOAT buffer views through vkd3d-proton. They now are
R32 texel buffers of three times the width, and their descriptors, grown
to 16 bytes for texel buffers, mark them. Fetches from such a descriptor
read the three components one by one, with an alpha of one, and size
queries divide by three.

Generated-by: LLM
